# What `scripts/materialize-gold-fixture.sh` copies, and what it becomes.
#
# `<source under test/fixtures/gold-loop/repo/>` <whitespace> `<destination in the
# materialized repository>`. Blank lines and `#` comments are ignored.
#
# THE SCRIPT REFUSES IN BOTH DIRECTIONS. A manifest line whose source is missing
# is a refusal, and — the one that actually bites — a file present under `repo/`
# that NO line names is also a refusal. Adding a file to the fixture and
# forgetting the manifest would otherwise materialize a silently incomplete
# repository, which is the failure mode a copy-the-whole-tree script cannot have
# and an explicit list can. The refusal is what buys the explicitness back.
#
# The one rename is why this file is not `cp -a`: `gitignore.in` must not hide
# `kata-out/` from kata's own tooling inside this checkout.

gitignore.in     .gitignore
README.md        README.md
kata/brief.md    kata/brief.md
src/tally.sh     src/tally.sh
tests/check.sh   tests/check.sh
tests/test_tail.sh  tests/test_tail.sh
